A||N||5||SloPonti||Getting ready to autocross the car this weekend-need some pointers!!!!!||||14||
Z||000000||SloPonti||05-31-2000||12:36 AM||||okay i am getting ready to autocross this weekend! i have done this once before so i am not totally new to it but my car was totally stock then! here is the car<BR>84 four banger<BR>auto trans<BR>polurathane moter and cradle mounts<BR>new shocks and struts<BR>new four wheel disk brakes<BR>new bearings<BR>new goodyear eagle hp tires  215/60/14 all the way around<BR>new motor-hooker header-holley tb-comp cam-accel wires-msd coil-ram air side scoop-gt stock dual exhaust<BR>polurathane control arm bushing<BR>new upper and lower ball joints<P>so what are some tips for racing!<BR>thanks<BR>Rob||||reg||14
Z||000001||Shiner||05-31-2000||01:02 AM||||Go really fast.  When something gets in your way, turn.||||reg||1
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||05-31-2000||01:13 AM||||Best advise I have gotten: Be smooth inside the car. Don't jerk the wheel and slam the gas or brake. Being slower in the car makes you faster. Look ahead and <B>know the course</B>... walk it several times and find the lines you need to keep the exit speed as high as possible. <P>Watch your tires. Get some shoe polish and mark the sidewall (only about 3 spots on each tire about 1/2" down the sidewall). Air up your tires a tad to keep them from rolling the sidewall under. I would say about 38 psi in the front and 40 psi(for a starting point) in the rear with those tires. Back to the shoe polish. You want the tire to roll about 1/4 inch on it's sidewall. If you go too far or not enough, remember it takes 3psi to move that point up or down 1/4 inch. You are going to have a "push" without a rear swaybar. To take some of this out you need to make the rear "loose". This is why the rear needs more psi than the front(and it has more weight). If the front pushes(I'm sure it will) take a couple psi out of the front tires.<P>Actually the best advise I have ever gotten: <B>Have fun</B>||||reg||1
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||05-31-2000||01:14 AM||||P.S. Those orange cones...don't hit them  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||80's BOY||06-01-2000||04:08 PM||||don't miss any gates....it makes you feel like an idiot in front of total strangers. DNF is nothing to be proud of!!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||DRH||06-01-2000||05:38 PM||||I have been in one autocross so far, so I am by no means an expert.<P>Memorizing the course beforehand and looking ahead during your run can not be stressed enough. I missed a gate and got the dreaded DNF the first run. The course looks different at speed and you won't have time to think about where to go next.<P>I'll second the comment on smoothness. My class was won by a guy that has done this for 12 years. He beat me by about 10 seconds (1:11 vs 1:21). Watching him run, the number one thing I noticed was how smooth everything was. He never seemed to have to make braking or steering corrections and always seemed to slow down JUST enough to make it. <P><BR>It is a LOT of FUN!!! Good luck!<BR>||||reg||14
